  "id": "visual-neglect",
  "term": "visual neglect",
  "definition": "Visual neglect is a disabling problem that can follow damage to the right hemisphere of the brain, in which a person shows a spatial bias in noticing visual information. It may be subtle or partly compensated, so it can be missed on simple paper-and-pencil testing, especially when attention demands are low.",
